studied by means of inclusive transverse momentum spectra and can be measured in the central events and does not depend on the determination of the reaction plane defined by the beam axis and the line of joining two centers of colliding nuclei. Anisotropic expansion in non-central events is described by the directed and elliptic flow components. The azimuthal distribution of particle in momentum space can be expanded in the form of Fourier series:

