Due to the upstream materials the photon undergo a conversion and scattering because of the large deflection. This affects the photon counting efficiency and purity of photon sample. The upstream material is described in terms of change in the occupancy, multihit probability, deviations of incoming particles. The distribution of \(\delta\eta\) (\(\eta_{clus}-\eta_{orig}\)) and \(\delta\phi\) (\(\phi_{clus}-\phi_{orig}\)) for the PMD only and for PMD in presence of all detectors in STAR experiment are shown in the Figure 3.18.

