\[P(m)={(m+k-1)!\over m!(k-1)!}{(\mu/k)^{m}\over(1+\mu/k)^{m+k}}\]

Where P(m) is normalised for \(0\leq m\leq\infty,\mu=<m>\). The NBD becomes a Poisson distribution in the limit \(k\longrightarrow\) infinity. The variance and the mean of the NBD is related to \(k\) by \(1/k=(\sigma^{2}/\mu^{2})-1/\mu\), where \(\mu\) is the mean and \(\sigma\) is the standard deviation of the distribution.

