The chiral symmetry is a fundamental (approximate) feature of the strong interaction but it has a firm observational basis only near the normal vacuum. It is therefore of interest to seek experimental information over a wider range of environments. Since high-energy nuclear collisions produce very hot and dense systems, it is natural to investigate whether they can be utilized for this purpose. It has long been speculated that the rapid expansion of the collision zone in heavy ion collisions, after an approximate restoration of

